cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the data it produces, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  agent-id-probe: passive, spec-anchored measurement of identity and authorization
  metadata in deployed AI agent endpoints
abstract: >-
  RFC 9728 section 7.6 places the secure determination of which authorization server
  belongs to a protected resource explicitly outside the specification's scope, names the
  resulting attack, and offers a single mitigation; the Model Context Protocol passes that
  decision to the client unchanged. agent-id-probe measures the decision surface this
  creates across deployed AI agent endpoints -- how many resources delegate to how many
  issuers, and how much of that delegation a client can verify from what the ecosystem
  publishes. Every check is bound to a normative sentence in a published specification
  (RFC 9728, RFC 8414, RFC 7515, RFC 8785, MCP Authorization, A2A Agent Card), and a check
  may report a failure only where it can cite a MUST -- a rule enforced in code rather than
  promised in prose. The instrument is passive and read-only: GET requests to well-known
  paths, no authentication, no writes, an enforced opt-out list, and all raw responses
  stored so any verdict can be re-scored offline.
type: software
